🕵️‍♀️ Marketing Detective
A polished, single-file detective game that teaches marketing analysis through investigation. Open a case file, gather evidence, and solve the real marketing mistake behind a failed campaign — built for Day 34 of the #60DaysOfClaudeAI challenge.
Overview
Marketing Detective turns marketing case studies into an interactive detective experience. Instead of reading a dry case study, you investigate one: flip evidence cards to reveal campaign metrics, customer comments, and social performance, then identify the primary marketing mistake before the case is closed.
Features
10 unique fictional cases — each with a different industry, objective, audience, channels, budget, metrics, and a distinct primary marketing mistake
Investigation Board — case overview presented as pinned index cards on a corkboard
Interactive Evidence Room — draggable, flip-to-reveal evidence cards (metrics, comments, social performance, clues)
Animated data bars for campaign metrics (reach, CTR, engagement, conversions, sales)
Solve the Case — multiple-choice diagnosis with distractor options pulled from other cases
Case Closed stamp animation with a correct/incorrect verdict
Learning Report — full explanation of the real mistake plus 3 suggested improvements
4 selectable color themes, including Claude Orange
Fully responsive, works on desktop and mobile
Tech Stack
Pure HTML, CSS, and Vanilla JavaScript
Zero external dependencies, zero build tools, zero backend
Single self-contained .html file — works fully offline, just open it in a browser
How to Use
Download marketing-detective.html
Open it directly in any modern browser (no server required)
Pick a color theme, open a case file, and start investigating
Case Flow
Case Assignment → Investigation Board → Evidence Room (drag + flip) → Solve the Case → Case Closed → Learning Report
Why This Project
Built as part of the #60DaysOfClaudeAI challenge — one polished, single-file web app per day, designed with Claude to sharpen both frontend craft and marketing/business thinking.
